  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe only requirement I see for `optgroup` is\n\n> An [optgroup](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-elements.html#the-optgroup-element) element is [expected](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#expected) to be rendered by displaying the element's [label](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-elements.html#attr-optgroup-label) attribute.\n\nwhich seems insufficient for what the tests expect.\n\nThe `option` element also has a rather curious sentence that I don't quite understand:\n\n> indented under its [optgroup](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-elements.html#the-optgroup-element) element if it has one\n\nShouldn't that be defined through CSS, if there's any indentation to be done at all? Also, if you render `option` like suggested in the surrounding sentence, you might well end up with a rendering that doesn't support pseudo-elements, so something is missing there as well.\n\ncc @mfreed7 @josepharhar @nt1m ",
